{"id":4010,"date":"2017-08-20T16:10:30","date_gmt":"2017-08-20T20:10:30","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=4010"},"modified":"2017-08-20T16:10:30","modified_gmt":"2017-08-20T20:10:30","slug":"riding-a-cable-ferry-at-lake-charlevoix","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2017\/08\/20\/riding-a-cable-ferry-at-lake-charlevoix\/","title":{"rendered":"Riding A &#8220;Cable&#8221; Ferry at Lake Charlevoix"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>Our road trip a few weeks ago took us up M-22 and M-119 through <a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2017\/08\/09\/part-2-nwest-michigan-road-trip-mushrooms-tunnels-bears-and-indians-oh-my\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Charlevoix and Petoskey and on up to the Mackinac Bridge and across to St. Ignace<\/a>. \u00a0On our way back down into the Lower Peninsula, we needed to head to Kalkaska on M-66 to visit my parents grave.<\/p>\n<p>This return trip took us to a delightful little <a href=\"http:\/\/www.visitcharlevoix.com\/Ironton-Ferry\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Village of Ironton<\/a> where there is a ferry that crosses the &#8220;narrows&#8221; of Lake Charlevoix giving riders a shortcut from Boyne City to Charlevoix.<\/p>\n<p>As we had already spent a thoroughly enjoyable time in <a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2017\/07\/24\/workampers-northwest-michigan-road-trip\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Charlevoix the previous night<\/a>, we instead crossed on the ferry and headed south on M-66 to Kalkaska.<\/p>\n<p>To get a better look at the area and be able to zoom in or out, <a href=\"https:\/\/www.google.com\/maps\/place\/Ironton,+MI+49727\/@45.2628473,-85.1740639,12.14z\/data=!4m5!3m4!1s0x4d4a949363887d29:0x48594783740db722!8m2!3d45.25611!4d-85.18667?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">click on this interactive map link<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/NarrowsCrossing.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4019\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/NarrowsCrossing.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1545\" height=\"872\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/NarrowsCrossing.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/NarrowsCrossing-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/NarrowsCrossing-768x433.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/NarrowsCrossing-1024x578.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1545px) 100vw, 1545px\" \/><\/a>\u00a0I thought the ferry was <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">so cool<\/span>. \u00a0A ferry boat has been crossing this narrows since 1883, with this present vessel being placed into service in 1925. \u00a0On most boats, ferry or otherwise, the captain (or pilot) not only controls the engine speed and direction, but also steers the boat by use of a rudder and\/or bow thruster engines\/props.<\/p>\n<p>With this ferry however, the craft is &#8220;driven&#8221; by propellers on each end (from one small diesel motor that runs in both directions) but the direction that the boat travels is guided along by a 3\/4&#8243; diameter steel cable that is secured at the ferry dock at each end. \u00a0There is no steering and there is no rudder.<\/p>\n<p>Back in the &#8220;old days&#8221; the passengers provided the power by pulling the boat along using hand-over-hand power on the cable.<\/p>\n<p>&#8220;How do boats navigate the narrows&#8221; you ask? \u00a0There is enough slack in the cable so that it is only above the surface of the water at each end and at the ferry boat itself. \u00a0Otherwise the cable drops to a depth of about 25&#8242; so that other watercraft can safely navigate.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_4013\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4013\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.30.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-4013 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.30.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.30.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.30-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.30-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.30-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-4013\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">The Ironton Ferry Boat<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p><iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/1PCaryXjYYo\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"><\/iframe><\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_4014\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4014\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.18.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-4014 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.18.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.18.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.18-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.18-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-17.01.18-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-4014\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Looking Across The Narrows of Lake Charlevoix at Ironton<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<figure id=\"attachment_4015\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4015\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.59.02.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-4015 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.59.02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.59.02.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.59.02-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.59.02-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.59.02-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-4015\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Waiting In Line to Board<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<figure id=\"attachment_4016\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4016\" style=\"width: 1440px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.53.53.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-4016 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.53.53-e1503257661488.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1440\" height=\"2560\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.53.53-e1503257661488.jpg 304w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.53.53-e1503257661488-169x300.jpg 169w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.53.53-e1503257661488-768x1365.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.53.53-e1503257661488-576x1024.jpg 576w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1440px) 100vw, 1440px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-4016\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">The Ferry Rate Chart<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<figure id=\"attachment_4018\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4018\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.17.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-4018 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.17.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.17.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.17-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.17-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.17-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-4018\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">The Ferry Has Departed<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<figure id=\"attachment_4017\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4017\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.42.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-4017 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.42.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.42.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.42-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.42-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-16.52.42-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-4017\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Placard Detailing The History of The Ferry<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>We are continually amazed and delighted at the opportunities that this workamping lifestyle affords us. \u00a0Although we were both born and raised in Michigan, we continue to be pleasantly surprised with all that this beautiful Water-Winter-Wonderland has to offer.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Our road trip a few weeks ago took us up M-22 and M-119 through Charlevoix and Petoskey and on up to the Mackinac Bridge and across to St. Ignace. \u00a0On our way back down into the Lower Peninsula, we needed to head to Kalkaska on M-66 to visit my parents grave. This return trip took &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2017\/08\/20\/riding-a-cable-ferry-at-lake-charlevoix\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading <span class=\"screen-reader-text\">Riding A &#8220;Cable&#8221; Ferry at Lake Charlevoix<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[19546,554707329],"tags":[554707411,554707407,554707434,18086,11110],"class_list":["post-4010","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-sightseeing","category-traveling","tag-charlevoix","tag-ferry","tag-ironton","tag-lake","tag-michigan"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4010","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=4010"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4010\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":4021,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4010\/revisions\/4021"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=4010"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=4010"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=4010"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}